{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1093979-help-on-a-true-fae-idea","id":1093979,"title":"Help on a True Fae idea.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-17T21:19:26-07:00","id":1093979,"title":"Help on a True Fae idea.","content":"A while ago, i thought up an idea for a True Fae and i want to know how to build it in the game. Basically, the Fae is called The Bloody Woman. She is a quite unusual fae due to the fact that she seems to like making bargains with mortals instead of kidnapping them. Her bargains tend to involve the Fae doing a favor for the mortal in exchange for the mortal doing something for her, which often involves kidnapping someone for Her to bring back to Arcadia or serving as one of her agents in the mortal realm. As you can guess, this has led her to have quite a few mortal minions. The consequences for violating your side of one of her bargains tend to be quite disastrous, often leading to death or disfigurement.<br /> <br /> The Fae first appeared in India in the 1800s where it haunted the roads looking for people to snatch. It was here where she gained her love for making bargains with humans after making a deal with a British Big Game Hunter to help him find a rare albino crocodile in exchange for the man's third finger, which she still keeps in a locket. To this day, she alternates from spending time in her realm in Arcadia and approaching select people for bargains.<br /> <br /> Besides building this Fae in game, I want help with determining how to develop her realm and what she should do to the poor souls trapped in her realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:21:17-07:00","id":1093992,"title":"","content":"Maybe this Gentry has an odd fixation with taking living things apart, but also has a weird notion of equivalent exchange? She might stalk her captives through the dark and lure them into traps that rip out both physical and metaphysical parts of the victims. After that, she replaces the missing parts with stuff from the Hedge and parts from other captives, all based on the types of bargains made. This creates patchwork changelings with a very Frankenstein feel. This would require a lot of crazy and decrepit surgery and sewing machines lying about, I think. The whole place would smell awful if she doesn't make any captives clean up the blood and gore.<br /> <br /> For stats, check out the Equinox Road supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:40:41-07:00","id":1094000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1093979-help-on-a-true-fae-idea?p=1093992#post1093992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this Gentry has an odd fixation with taking living things apart, but also has a weird notion of equivalent exchange? She might stalk her captives through the dark and lure them into traps that rip out both physical and metaphysical parts of the victims. After that, she replaces the missing parts with stuff from the Hedge and parts from other captives, all based on the types of bargains made. This creates patchwork changelings with a very Frankenstein feel. This would require a lot of crazy and decrepit surgery and sewing machines lying about, I think. The whole place would smell awful if she doesn't make any captives clean up the blood and gore.<br /> <br /> For stats, check out the Equinox Road supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>The surgery concept is a great idea. I was thinking of making one of her human minions not changed into a changeling being a guy with a heavily scarred face. Perhaps the Fae disfigured him to make him pay for failing to uphold his end of the bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}